	(text_box "KILL SWITCH DELAY NOTES\n\nProvides a ~1.65s delay on the 12V input and scales it to 2.52V to safely drive the 3.3V Schmitt trigger (U12).\n\nR13 (15k) is small compared to R12 (120k) and R14 (36k) to prevent circuit loading, ensuring the input successfully climbs past the 2.0V threshold.\n\nC27 must be a 25V Conductive Polymer capacitor to eliminate DC bias capacitance loss and allow low resistor values that resist PCB contamination."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.126 134.5715 0)
		(size 51.836 30.5285)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5482ee8d-28d0-462a-96a0-64d47f0201c0")
	)
